  "summary": "The study prepared Ti3C2Tx nanosheets by 40% HF etching of Ti3AlC2 followed by TMAOH exfoliation, then vacuum-filtered membranes with boron quantum-dot (BQD) pillars. Five fabricated electrode materials are explicitly distinguishable: a BQDs reference electrode, pure Ti3C2Tx membrane, and BQDs(5)-, BQDs(10)-, and BQDs(15)-Ti3C2Tx membranes. BQDs(10)-Ti3C2Tx is the headline and best performer, delivering 524 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121 in 6 M H2SO4; its symmetric PVA/H2SO4 flexible device reports 552 mF cm\u22122 at 1.25 mA cm\u22122. Numerical capacitances for pure Ti3C2Tx and the 5 wt.% and 15 wt.% BQD composites are not printed in the supplied text, despite their plotted comparisons."
}